WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.164
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:08.862
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.162 --> 00:00:16.586
Unit eleven: Interdisciplinary Studies. Today you will describe dynamic processes with present participles as adjectives.

4
00:00:16.886 --> 00:00:19.527
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.653
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.517 --> 00:00:25.959
Interdisciplinary.

7
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:31.922
Interdisciplinary means combining methods and insights from several academic fields.

8
00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:35.468
Climate science is inherently interdisciplinary.

9
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:38.956
Your turn. Say: Interdisciplinary.

10
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.196
Interdisciplinary.

11
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.114
Synthesis.

12
00:00:46.117 --> 00:00:50.125
Synthesis means the combination of distinct ideas into a coherent whole.

13
00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:54.086
The book offers a synthesis of psychology and economics.

14
00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:57.312
Your turn. Say: Synthesis.

15
00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:01.446
Synthesis.

16
00:01:02.183 --> 00:01:03.510
Cross-pollination.

17
00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:08.943
Cross-pollination means the mutual enrichment of fields through exchange of ideas.

18
00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:13.860
Cross-pollination between design and medicine produced new devices.

19
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.300
Your turn. Say: Cross-pollination.

20
00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.506
Cross-pollination.

21
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.100
Framework.

22
00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:27.428
Framework means a conceptual structure used to analyse a problem.

23
00:01:28.017 --> 00:01:30.991
Each discipline brings its own analytical framework.

24
00:01:31.583 --> 00:01:33.818
Your turn. Say: Framework.

25
00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:37.749
Framework.

26
00:01:38.483 --> 00:01:39.368
Boundary.

27
00:01:40.383 --> 00:01:43.637
Boundary means a dividing line between areas of knowledge.

28
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.631
The most exciting research happens at disciplinary boundaries.

29
00:01:48.217 --> 00:01:50.857
Your turn. Say: Boundary.

30
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:54.689
Boundary.

31
00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:56.660
Collaboration.

32
00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:01.484
Collaboration means joint work towards a shared intellectual goal.

33
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:05.418
Effective collaboration requires a shared vocabulary.

34
00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:08.808
Your turn. Say: Collaboration.

35
00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:12.865
Collaboration.

36
00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:14.641
Holistic.

37
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:19.809
Holistic means considering the whole system rather than isolated parts.

38
00:02:20.417 --> 00:02:22.753
Public health demands a holistic approach.

39
00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:26.153
Your turn. Say: Holistic.

40
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.001
Holistic.

41
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.902
Convergence.

42
00:02:32.917 --> 00:02:36.530
Convergence means the process of separate fields coming together.

43
00:02:37.117 --> 00:02:41.136
The convergence of biology and computing created bioinformatics.

44
00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.797
Your turn. Say: Convergence.

45
00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:48.704
Convergence.

46
00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.011
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:59.393
Visal, you've chosen 'urban heat' for your research project. Isn't that just a geography topic?

48
00:03:00.483 --> 00:03:10.647
Not really. A converging field draws on economics, biology, and sociology, as well as geography.

49
00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.028
Why does it need so many disciplines?

50
00:03:15.117 --> 00:03:24.456
Rising temperatures affect health, energy costs and inequality at once. No single framework captures that complexity.

51
00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:28.293
Isn't collaboration across fields difficult?

52
00:03:29.383 --> 00:03:37.307
It can be. Competing definitions are a real obstacle, so the first task is agreeing on a shared vocabulary.

53
00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:40.164
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:41.017 --> 00:03:44.804
Grammar focus: Present participle as adjective.

55
00:03:45.104 --> 00:03:46.256
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:51.237
A converging field draws on economics, biology, and sociology.

57
00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:55.148
Rising temperatures affect health and inequality.

58
00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:59.756
The emerging discipline of bioinformatics is growing rapidly.

59
00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:13.000
Present participles describe nouns in an active, ongoing process: a converging field, rising temperatures. Compare past participles, which describe a completed or passive state: a converged system.

60
00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:18.550
Be careful! Don't say: An emerged field links biology and data.

61
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.496
Say: An emerging field links biology and data.

62
00:04:24.796 --> 00:04:27.551
Use the -ing participle for an ongoing process.

63
00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:31.065
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:31.867 --> 00:04:33.715
Beyond Disciplinary Walls.

65
00:04:34.015 --> 00:04:39.150
Universities have traditionally organised knowledge into separate, clearly bounded departments.

66
00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:43.956
Many pressing problems, however, refuse to respect such boundaries.

67
00:04:44.967 --> 00:04:52.493
A converging field draws on economics, biology, and sociology to explain phenomena that no single discipline can.

68
00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:59.110
This cross-pollination of frameworks tends to produce more holistic, and often more innovative, solutions.

69
00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:05.524
Yet genuine convergence demands patient collaboration and a willingness to question one's own assumptions.

70
00:05:06.633 --> 00:05:10.426
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:11.283 --> 00:05:15.512
A blank field draws on economics, biology, and sociology.

72
00:05:15.812 --> 00:05:19.674
A, converged. B, converging. C, converge.

73
00:05:23.233 --> 00:05:25.210
The answer is B: converging.

74
00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.953
'Temperatures that are rising' can be shortened to blank.

75
00:05:29.253 --> 00:05:34.242
A, risen temperatures. B, rising temperatures. C, rise temperatures.

76
00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:40.392
The answer is B: rising temperatures.

77
00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:45.001
Considering the whole system rather than isolated parts is blank.

78
00:05:45.301 --> 00:05:48.896
A, holistic. B, bounded. C, fragmented.

79
00:05:52.433 --> 00:05:54.514
The answer is A: holistic.

80
00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:58.787
Which phrase describes a completed, passive state?

81
00:05:59.087 --> 00:06:04.854
A, a developing theory. B, an established theory. C, an emerging theory.

82
00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.108
The answer is B: an established theory.

83
00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:15.457
According to the reading, what does genuine convergence demand?

84
00:06:15.757 --> 00:06:20.850
A, patient collaboration. B, separate departments. C, a single framework.

85
00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.212
The answer is A: patient collaboration.

86
00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.702
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:36.454
What is one advantage of studying a problem from multiple disciplines?

88
00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:54.634
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:54.934 --> 00:07:34.595
One major advantage is that you see connections a single discipline would miss. Rising sea levels, for example, are not only an environmental issue but also an economic and social one. A team combining engineers, economists and sociologists can therefore design more realistic solutions. Admittedly, interdisciplinary work can be slow, because experts use different methods and terminology. Even so, for complex modern problems, I believe the benefits clearly outweigh the costs.

90
00:07:34.895 --> 00:07:36.628
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:37.517 --> 00:07:42.061
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present participle as adjective.

92
00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:47.347
Today's value is open-mindedness. Listen to new ideas before you judge them.

93
00:07:47.647 --> 00:07:50.288
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

94
00:07:50.588 --> 00:07:53.287
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

